  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note-header",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": { "x": 20, "y": -180 },
      "data": {
        "label": "Sinnamary Mangrove Dynamics — Phase 1",
        "params": {
          "text": "# Sinnamary Mangrove Dynamics — Phase 1\n\n**Goal:** Map mangrove extent and multi-year change along the Sinnamary coast (French Guiana) using **Sentinel-1 SAR + LULC fusion** — no atmospheric correction blockers, all sources free, no authentication required.\n\n**AOI:** lon [-53.30, -52.60], lat [4.40, 5.50] (~9 500 km², mangrove coast + Sinnamary watershed)\n\n## Pipeline\n🟦 **Data acquisition (left)** : Sentinel-1 RTC backscatter (Microsoft Planetary Computer, no auth) → 7 derived polarization features. ESA WorldCover 2021 (explicit `Mangroves` class = ground truth). io-lulc-annual-v02 for 2017 and 2024 (annual change basis).\n\n🟧 **Change detection (right)** : geo_time_align reprojects 2024 LULC onto 2017's grid and computes per-pixel class change + change mask.\n\n## Expected outputs\n- S1 polarization-feature preview (R=RVI, G=NRPB, B=PDI)\n- ESA WorldCover 2021 mangrove map\n- io-lulc 2024 land cover\n- Change mask 2017→2024 (mangrove expansion + forest loss)\n\n## Next phase\nTemplate #16 couples upstream orpaillage (io-lulc Bare ground) with downstream Sinnamary turbidity (Naïades stations).",
          "width": 1340,
          "height": 320,
          "fontSize": 13,
          "color_index": 4
        }
      },
      "width": 1340,
      "height": 320
    },

    {
